.TH CHOWN 1
.SH NAME
chown \- change a file's owner and group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chown
.IR uid [: gid ]
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chown
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It gives
.I path
the owner
.I uid
and the group
.I gid
(the same number as
.I uid
when not given). Root only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
chown 0:100 /tmp/grp.txt
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chmod (1),
.BR id (1),
.BR sh (1)
.SH BUGS
Numbers only, not names; one path at a time.
